  singular-value diagnostics and >3 m warning.
- ATE RMSE/mean/median/max/std, endpoint displacement vector error, 10/25/50/100 m
  RPE (translation %, yaw deg/100 m), evo SE3 ATE cross-check assertion <1 mm.
- Scan-header SLERP and translation interpolation, no per-point deskew;
  incremental weighted voxels preserve mean relative time and header stamp.
- Common ENU GNSS XY crop, 0.1 m voxels, local radius 0.3 m Gaussian MME
  and minimum covariance eigenvalue MPV; coverage counts included.
- First/last 15 s bidirectional overlap distances, 1 m overlap gate,
  median/p95 and >0.2 m ratio; coverage fractions accompany statistics.
- All-run orchestration, tables, Agg/200 dpi color-friendly plots and
  source checksum verification. Separate independent artifact audit.

## Historical loop-factor limitation

Inspection of "'`tools/record_traj.py`, run logs, run metadata and upstream
loop implementation confirms the saved marker callback stores only the
maximum edge count. It does not retain endpoint identities, timestamps,
marker messages or a graph. The final transformations PCD stores poses,
not loop-factor connectivity. Therefore actual keyframe pairs and their
<2 m GT distances cannot be established from retained artifacts.
The evaluation will label these as NOT_RECORDED, never invent pairs or
call proximity candidates true positives. Existing experiments are not
replayed because that would create different nondeterministic runs.

Online poses already contain corrections from earlier loops. Their ATE
versus final keyframes is useful but is not per-factor before/after ATE.

## Direct validation

- Unit tests restore a known rigid transform and a known 3D lever arm
  with varied six-axis orientations; enforce determinant +1 and no scaling.
- Tests cover GT gaps/interpolation, zero-error ATE and evo agreement,
  exact straight-line RPE and 10% scale error, ENU axis directions,
  weighted voxel time preservation, plane covariance, symmetric overlap,
  and scan parity/SLERP/provenance.
- Full existing and new test suite: **47 passed**.
- Actual-data metrics, map tables, figures and visual inspection remain
  pending the GNSS sigma scope decision; they have not been claimed complete.

## Interpretation (three lines)

1. All-axis 5 cm GNSS quality filtering leaves no GT, so no actual ATE/RPE comparison is yet defensible under that interpretation.
2. Horizontal-only filtering matches the task'"'s stated 1.3–1.5 cm precision, but vertical uncertainty must be disclosed if authorized.
3. Fitness=0.5 loop true/false-positive validation requires historical edge identities that TASK-04 did not save; event counts and small endpoint distance cannot substitute.
